## Alignment with independent research

Daniel's preparation-proposal assessment supports a bounded Fable experiment within Reiyah,
without replacing the product mission. Its selected preparation grid's 20 outcomes all abstain;
89..2661 additions are neither a decision-flip result nor physical-risk or human-effort bounds.
Keep fixed-comparison uncertainty separate from evaluation-definition sensitivity and deliberate
configuration changes. Fable owns that experiment and corrections; Engine owns inspection,
custody, admission and common operands. No Fable source or status changed.

An ordinary preparation sweep is a serious first baseline. Bell et al.'s
[Modeling the Machine Learning Multiverse](https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.05985v2), NeurIPS 2022,
is relevant prior work on sensitivity to ML choices; it does not certify Reiyah's physical
alternatives or exact bounds. A retrospective annotation-conditional experiment cannot supply
the missing independent human references here. Buyer demand and state-of-the-art claims remain
hypotheses. No outreach is authorized.

